Note :- Anything that we  will do in HLD is to make our application scale better. 

-We will be creating a project, and understand what components we need to scale our application to millions of users. 

### 1. Simple Client-Server Architecture :-
Structure :- 
 - Client tier :- Client1 : WebBrowser Client2: MobileApp 
 - Web-Server tier : Web-Server

 - And we know from our last lecture that client never sends the request direct to the server it sends through the DNS. 
 - So firstly client request to DNS server and then DNS response the IP address. 
   - DNS server has Mapping table include the URL and IP section. 
   - After receiving the response from the DNS, client then make http request to the web-server.
   - Then WebServer will return response after processing. 
   - Response may be html page which user want to render, JSON, etc

UnderStanding that what actually the http request intake :- 
While api calling we have the different http headers, and the header have their body. 
  1. Different types of http calls are :- Post, Get, Put,etc
  2. url : www.example.com
  3. Headers :- 
    1. Request-JSON
    2. Client credential's
  4. Body : json format

- So we send these details while http request to the server. After this server process the request. What would be that processing? Processing may be fetching some details, to store the data, do some computation. 

If using this architecture and we built some application like instagram,etc Then it will be not able to handle the much of users because :- 
  - 1. Here we are having only one server, so it is possible that there must be Database in that server. As we know from the definition of the server that it is speclized computer which is deploy on Internet which handle the server calls.
   - To scale up the application we need to put our database to the another server. 

### Introduced DB layer in  Simple Client-Server Architecture :-  
Structure :- 
 - Client tier :- Client1 : WebBrowser Client2: MobileApp 
 - Web-Server tier : Web-Server
 - DB(Database) tier : DB-Server

Now How the calling will be happened :- 
 1. Client to DNS (req)
 2. DNS to Client (res)
 3. Client to Web-Server (req)
 4. web-server to Datbase (req->processing needed to Webserver)
 5. Database to Web-server (res)
 6. Web-server to Client (res)

 Note :- Database apne processing mai kya karega may be write , kuchh details fetch karega,etc

 So using this architecture we can able to handle the more user as if wants to scale-up the web-server we simple add new web server and if want to sacle the database then we can simply add new database. 

 ##### Which Db to Use? 
 We mainly divide the database into two parts as : 
 1. Relational Database 
   - This type of db are sql based means we can apply qurry over the data. 
   - Different DB : MySql, PostGreSql, OracleSql, etc
   - We have row-col and we have different qerry on the rwo-col or table.

   - So why NRD comes as we know that every data cannot be structured. Like if we want to store the JSON format to the RD then it would be having the differnt complication.  
 2. Non Relational Database 
   - We divide the NDR into four parts :-
   1. Key-Value Store :- 
    - Just like we use the map in python  it is similar to that. We can store the data in different format as string to string, string to integer, string to double, etc
    - Ex Amazon Dynamo DB
   2. Column Based Store :- Ex Casandra DB 
   3. Document Based Store : MongoDb 
   4. Graph store :- GraphQl
     - like following and follors based dierected and Undirected Graph, for storing this type of graph we need the graph store DB. 

    What are the factor on which we decide which type of DB we need to choose b/w the RD and NRD? 
    - Criteria 1 :- 
      1. Is our data is structered data
      2. Is we need qurry on our stored data
      If yes then we can RD. 
      - If Not stuctured :- Then we go for the NRD.

    - Criteria 2 :- Response Time
      - If having an application where need fast response, for those we prefer the NRD. Because in NRD we are having low latency. We will be seeing this in details further, 

  #### Muliple Server :- 
  - As this architecture is optimized then before and capable to manage the user upto 30k because after sometime Our webserver is resources reached to maximum. 
   - If many user sends the request at same time then our server ram gets used and reached to its maximum then we need to do the scaling of the server(vertical or horizontal).  
    - Vertical scaling : Specification of server ko increase karna 
      limitation : 
       1. Isko kuchh samay tak he bada sakte hai, kuchh samay baad hamko rukna hoga
       2. So yaha ek he server hai, so if it fails our application stop working also called SPOF(Single Point OF Failure)
    - Horizontal Scaling :- Attaching new server
  
  - Modified Structure after horizontal scaling :- 
    - Client tier :- Client1 : WebBrowser Client2: MobileApp 
    - Web-Server tier : Web-Server1 , Web-Server2
    - DB(Database) tier : DB-Server

    
  - Now user can request any of the server, some request is handled by WebServer1 and some by webServer2. -> By doing so we decrese the load from the server. 
  
  - How we will be decide that In which server we have to send the request and who will be deciding this ? Means pahle jab client se request karte tab DNS hamko IP address lakar deta tha WebServer1 ka lakin ab kis Webserver ka IP la kar dega? Jiska ka bhi IP lakar dega then us case mai saari request toh waha chali jayegi
   - Load Balancer :- 
     - Load balancer is responsible for deciding that on which server we have to send the request. 
     - So ab client LB par request hit karega, aur LB decide karega ki usko request kaha bhejna hai, webServer1 par ki webServer2 par. 
     - So its been  tracking the servers and if any server have the load then it sends the current request to next/another server attached. 
     - We will be learning it in detail when we learning the LB architecture -> algo used etc 
    
  #### Load Balancer also introduced  :- 
  - Modified Structure after horizontal scaling :- 
    - Client tier :- Client1 : WebBrowser Client2: MobileApp 
    - Load Balancer 
    - Web-Server tier : Web-Server1 , Web-Server2
    - DB(Database) tier : DB-Server

  Now How the calling will be happened :- 
    1. Client to DNS (req)
    2. DNS to Client (res) : returns the IP of load-balancer
    3. Client to Load-balancer (req) : 
    4. Load-balancer to WebServer (req -> using private IP)
    4. web-server to Datbase (req)
    5. Database to Web-server (res)
    6. Web-server to Client (res)

    - Private beacuse we donot want anyother one to interact with our server. We want that if any want interact with our server then it must come through the Load-balancer. 
     - So LB ke pass public IP hai, anyone can call our LB. 

    - Ab ham server ko asaani se bada sakte hai if needed in future. 

    limitation with our database of current structure :-
    - We are having the single DB if its gets failed then what we will be doing (SPOF), then our application will unable to work or stop working. OR We lost our users data. 
    -> Introduced the database Scaling 

    #### DB Scaling :- 
    -  Modified Structure :- 
      - Client tier :- Client1 : WebBrowser Client2: MobileApp 
      - Load Balancer 
      - Web-Server tier : Web-Server1 , Web-Server2
      - DB(Database) tier : DB-Server 
    
      ##### Master Slave Architecture (Data backup) :- 
      - Responsible to communicate with server to database(multiple)  
      - What is Master-slave architecture and how is it helping in the data-replication? 
        - Master DB 
        - Slave DB :- slaveDb1, slaveDb2, slaveDb3

        Database Qurry means it can be read or write only two type of qurry will be there. Read qurry includes only select and write qurry includes insert, delete, update, etc. 
        - Write qurry will be perform on the Master DB and Read qurry will be perform on any of the slave. 

        How this architecture will work? 
        Master DB function:- The data available on the master DB will be replicate time to time on the Slaves Db we have available. 
        When it will replicate data? 
         1. Whenever the write operation perform on the master Db. 
         2. Time to Time replication, write operation aane ke baad turant replicate n kare, thoda ruke kuchh aur agar write operation hai toh unko bhi le le aur data replicate karle. 

        Slaves :-
        - responsible for performing the read qurry, means when demand for fetching some data from Db that will be performed here. 
        - So we may have the more than one slave then for that condition we need to intoduced Load-Balancer(LB). -> for deciding which slave to execute for qurry. 
      
      - We have been doing this for the data-replication, if any of DB gets currpted/crash then in that case we can recover our data from other slaves. 
      - What happend if master DB get crashed as we having only one masterDb. or When MasterDb get's the write operation before being updated in the slaves it get's crashed then what to do? (called STALE Data).
       - Then kisi ek mai se ham master bana denge. Which slave will become the next master slave for that we have different algorithum such as Voting Algorithum. 
       - We will be make the masterDb for  temporary period of time, till our Master DB will be Up again. or Deploy new master. We do this because slave DB is not that powerful and MasterDb has more functionalities.

      - This way replicate the data to protect from the data loss. 

  ### Added Master-Slave  
  Structure 
    - Client tier :- Client1 : WebBrowser Client2: MobileApp 
    - Load Balancer 
    - Web-Server tier : Web-Server1 , Web-Server2
    - DB(Database) tier : Master-Slave (db scaling)

Note :- Removed the SPOF (Single Point Of Failure) from our simple Architecture. 

- Think and Answer :- 
    We are having the more limitation left to scale our architecture to millions of users. We have the client side rendering languages like html/css/js and Server side rendering languages java,python, etc So we are JS language for the all the logic implementation, so " why we need the server layer? Why client is not communicate with dataBase directly?"
     - Database got exposed, and anyone can access the database and change credential of our database. 
     - Cannot have the authentication 

  ### Introduced Cache 
  - Cache is faster then database, so opertaion like read and write will be done faster on the database. 
  - Cache basically reduce the qurry related to database. 
  
  Logically placement of cache:-
   Components :- 
    - WebServer
    - Cache
    - Database 

  - It  is placed between the Webserver and Database, it means when webServer want to make a request , request first go to the cache if the data related to req  found then it sends the respose directly to the WebServer.
   - So if we try to hit the database again and again it will consume time. 
  - If cache has not the data then cache will request to db and then db response back, this is called the Cache Miss. 
  - Cash Hit :-  Found the data on the cache.

  - Cache also includes the different algorithum like Cache Eviction Algorithum, this algo says that if cache got full then which data will be released to put new data, see in detail in cache architecture. 

  New Structure of Architecture :-  
    - Client tier :- Client1 : WebBrowser Client2: MobileApp 
    - Load Balancer 
    - Web-Server tier : Web-Server1 , Web-Server2
    - Cache tier : cache (Directly attached with Webserver)
    - DB(Database) tier : Master-Slave (db scaling) -> (Directly attached with Webserver)

  - Now we improve the Latency -> If user wants data then user ka data fast de payenge.

  ### Intoduced CDN(Content Delivery Network)
  - If the application has more static content like html, css, js, images,etc hamko pata ye dynamic bhi ho sakta but if hamko same contents ko show karna hai then We try to avoid the server hit again and again in this case. It slow down process as we call server then server req the cache or DB for the data to load. 
   -> To avoid this we Introduced CDN.
  - CDN is third party vendor, means isko ham khid nahi banate isko integrate karte just like we integrated the DNS. 
  - It is like a proxy means client ko lagta hai ki wo ek server se baat karta hai, actually wo baat karta hai CDN se and client will be thinking that it gets the response from the server. 
   - So CDN act like a server but actually it is not a server.

  - We have different CDN available :- 
    - Amazon : CloudFront
    - Akamai

    so agar hamko contents ko load karwana hai apne application par then ham directly clients se CDN ko call karte hai, aur wo as response hamko Data de deta hai. 
    
    CDN efficency :- 
    - Graphical location of CDN matters

  New Structure of Architecture :-  
    - Client tier :- Client1 : WebBrowser Client2: MobileApp 
    - CDN : (Directly attached with Client)
    - Load Balancer 
    - Web-Server tier : Web-Server1 , Web-Server2
    - Cache tier : cache (Directly attached with Webserver)
    - DB(Database) tier : Master-Slave (db scaling) -> (Directly attached with Webserver)
  
  How CDN load the data fastly? 
  - When integrate the cdn to our application then we have to make change in the DNS. The mapping table of DNS will updating the URL and Ip address of the CDN. 
  - Calls we need to make to load the data on application :- 
     1. Client to CDN(req)
     2. CDN to Client (res)
     3. Client to CDN (req)
     4. cdn to Client (res)

### Autoscaling of the Server
 - Autoscalling of the server is not possible in the Updated Architecture till now. 
 - limitations :- Autoscaling not possible , Autoscaling means if load bad gaya hamare server par then apne aap ek naya server introduce nahi hoga or if users kam ho gaye then apne aap server kam nahi ho jayega. 
  - Because we know that ki har ek chiz ki cost hoti hai. 
  - We will be having the CDN only in case if our application is capable of generating that amount of money as cdn is costly. So jitani baar cdn hit hoga utna uske according charges then padte hai. We need optimized the cost. 

- How can we do the AutoScaling ? 
  - Sticky Session :- means aisa architecture state par dependent hai(Statful Architecture).
  - Client Sessions :- 
    - Example (Sticky Session) :- Lets say we have the user1 and user1 request for the web-server1 (we have LB and so architecture jo hamare pass hota hai). Client Sessions basically kuchh asise chize hoti hai, jo web-server ko client ke baare mai store karke rakhna hota hai. Stored Info like :- 
    - sign-up request of the plateform -> Who will be stored signup details?
    - After sign-up user1 do req2 to Web-server for seeing the story, then now server will try authenticate the server -> Server will look user1 in the session. If have the details in the session then we will allow user to see the story. 

    - We are having the multiple servers So if the session is stored in one of the server1 and we do req2 to another server then What Happend? 
      - Server2 will not have the info about the session of req1. So server2 will decline the request2. -> Resposne : "User not found". This all is called the Stickt Session.

    Solution :-  We need to redirect all the request of the user1 to server1(jaha session stored hai). Server2 par request redirect nahi kar sakte kyuki wo user pahchanne se mana kar dega. 
    
    Client Session :- Client information that a server needs to store on it, for the identification of the client/user for next time, that will call Client Session. 

    - Http protocol are sessionless(stateless) means inke pass client ki koi bhi information nahi hoti. So har ek request unique hai, server ko har baar ek nayi request milti hai means server ko pata nahi hota hai jo info uske paas aaya eo existing user ka hai ya nahi. 

    - So stateful arachiture are not good as here users become dependant on the server. To solve this issue we migrate from the StateFul Architecture to Statless Architecture.

    - What is StateLess Architecture?
